# AM3 candidate manifest. Frozen candidate of the AM3 unit (the separate Pocket entry point, the wake admission, the
# AM2 gate carry-in fixes, the standalone portability work, the Pocket install/migration tests, docs and scripts),
# after the AM3 gate fixes F1 (the input is submitted for the person the confirming read validated, and an identity that
# changes between the two reads cancels the admission), F2 (`watchFrom` named correctly in the docs and asserted), F3
# (the pending short-circuit test renamed to what it proves, the duplicate-event case split out) and F4 (the refused
# enable also asserts that the held-back state was never read).
# The AM1 manifest test/evidence/candidate.sha256 and the AM2 manifest test/evidence/am2-candidate.sha256 are retained
# unchanged as their records; AM3 deliberately changes exactly 14 of the AM2 manifest's 27 entries (verified with
# `sha256sum -c packages/agent-mail-identity/test/evidence/am2-candidate.sha256` from the workspace root):
# src/am-cli.ts, src/index.ts, src/watcher.ts, test/am-cli.test.ts, test/delivery.test.ts, test/durable.test.ts,
# test/watcher.test.ts, test/fixtures/am-fixture.mjs, scripts/check-boundaries.mjs, scripts/unavailable-gate.mjs,
# package.json, tsconfig.json, README.md and CONTRACT.md.
